 practiceQ.push(...[
["Which description best defines a clean surgical wound?","स्वच्छ शल्यक्रिया घाउको सही परिभाषा कुन हो?",["An uninfected operative wound with no inflammation and no entry into respiratory, alimentary, genital or urinary tracts","A wound with pus and established infection","A wound in which the respiratory tract is entered under controlled conditions","A wound with major accidental contamination"],0,"A clean wound is an uninfected operative wound with no inflammation and no entry into the respiratory, alimentary, genital or urinary tracts.","स्वच्छ घाउमा संक्रमण वा सूजन हुँदैन र श्वास, पाचन, जनन वा मूत्रमार्गमा प्रवेश गरिएको हुँदैन।","General Surgery"],
["A clean-contaminated surgical wound is one in which:","Clean-contaminated शल्यक्रिया घाउ भन्नाले कुन अवस्था बुझिन्छ?",["There is established pus formation","A respiratory, alimentary, genital or urinary tract is entered under controlled conditions without unusual contamination","There is gross spillage or major break in sterile technique","The wound is caused by an old untreated injury"],1,"A clean-contaminated wound involves controlled entry into a body tract that normally contains microorganisms, without unusual contamination.","सामान्यतया सूक्ष्मजीव हुने शरीरको मार्गमा नियन्त्रित रूपमा प्रवेश गरिएको तर असामान्य दूषण नभएको घाउ clean-contaminated हो।","General Surgery"],
["Which situation best describes a contaminated surgical wound?","Contaminated शल्यक्रिया घाउलाई कुन अवस्थाले राम्रोसँग वर्णन गर्छ?",["A clean elective incision with no inflammation","A closed wound with no entry into a body tract","Major break in sterile technique or gross spillage from the gastrointestinal tract","An old wound with established infection and pus"],2,"A contaminated wound may involve a major break in sterile technique, gross gastrointestinal spillage or acute non-purulent inflammation.","Sterile विधिमा ठूलो त्रुटि, पाचननलीको सामग्री धेरै पोखिनु वा तीव्र तर पीप नभएको सूजन भए contaminated wound हुन सक्छ।","General Surgery"],
["A dirty or infected surgical wound is characterized by:","Dirty वा infected शल्यक्रिया घाउको विशेषता के हो?",["A completely clean elective incision","Controlled entry into the gastrointestinal tract","A minor break in sterile technique only","Existing clinical infection, pus or devitalized tissue at the operative site"],3,"Dirty or infected wounds have established infection or devitalized tissue at the time of surgery.","शल्यक्रियाको समयमा नै संक्रमण, पीप वा मरेको तन्तु भएको घाउ dirty/infected मानिन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["What is the main purpose of a surgical safety time-out immediately before incision?","चिरा लगाउनुअघि गरिने surgical safety time-out को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["To confirm the correct patient, procedure and operative site with the team","To estimate the duration of the operation","To decide the patient's discharge date","To replace the need for informed consent"],0,"A team time-out helps verify the correct patient, procedure and site before the procedure begins.","Time-out ले शल्यक्रिया सुरु गर्नुअघि सही बिरामी, सही प्रक्रिया र सही स्थान भएको टोलीबाट पुष्टि गराउँछ।","General Surgery"],
["Before a planned operation, which action best supports correct patient identification?","नियोजित शल्यक्रियाअघि सही बिरामी पहिचान गर्न कुन कार्य उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Identify the patient by bed number only","Use at least two approved patient identifiers and match them with the records","Ask another patient to confirm the name","Rely only on the patient's room location"],1,"Use two approved identifiers, such as full name and date of birth or a unique hospital number, according to facility policy.","अस्पतालको नीतिअनुसार पूरा नाम र जन्ममिति वा विशिष्ट अस्पताल नम्बरजस्ता दुई स्वीकृत पहिचान प्रयोग गरी अभिलेखसँग मिलाउनुहोस्।","General Surgery"],
["Which statement about informed consent for surgery is correct?","शल्यक्रियाका लागि informed consent सम्बन्धी कुन भनाइ सही हो?",["Consent may be obtained from any visitor","Consent is unnecessary for a planned operation","The patient should receive understandable information and give consent voluntarily, with capacity assessed as appropriate","A signature alone replaces discussion"],2,"Valid consent requires understandable information, voluntariness and decision-making capacity; a signature alone is not enough.","वैध सहमतिका लागि बुझिने जानकारी, स्वेच्छा र निर्णय क्षमता आवश्यक हुन्छ; हस्ताक्षर मात्र पर्याप्त हुँदैन।","General Surgery"],
["Why are surgical swab and instrument counts performed?","शल्यक्रियामा gauze र instrument count किन गरिन्छ?",["To calculate blood pressure","To estimate wound healing time","To select the type of anaesthesia","To reduce the risk of items being unintentionally retained in the patient"],3,"Counts help prevent retention of swabs, needles or instruments in the patient after surgery.","शल्यक्रियापछि gauze, सुई वा उपकरण बिरामीको शरीरभित्र छुट्न नदिन count गरिन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["What is the principal purpose of incentive spirometry after selected operations?","केही शल्यक्रियापछि incentive spirometry को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["To encourage deep breaths and help reduce postoperative lung complications","To measure urine output","To remove fluid from the stomach","To assess wound strength"],0,"Incentive spirometry encourages sustained deep inspiration and may help reduce atelectasis in selected patients when used with a broader respiratory-care plan.","यसले गहिरो सास लिन प्रोत्साहन गर्छ र अन्य श्वाससम्बन्धी हेरचाहसँगै केही बिरामीमा फोक्सो खुम्चिने समस्या घटाउन मद्दत गर्न सक्छ।","General Surgery"],
["Which postoperative measure helps reduce the risk of venous stasis in an eligible patient?","उपयुक्त शल्यक्रियापछिको बिरामीमा venous stasis घटाउन कुन उपाय उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["Prolonged bed rest without movement","Early mobilization as prescribed and clinically safe","Restricting all leg movement","Keeping the patient seated continuously"],1,"Early, safe mobilization supports venous return; use it alongside other prescribed thrombosis-prevention measures.","सुरक्षित र समयमै हिँडडुल गर्दा शिराबाट रगत फर्कन सहयोग हुन्छ; चिकित्सकले तोकेका अन्य thrombosis रोकथामका उपाय पनि अपनाउनुपर्छ।","General Surgery"],
["What is the main purpose of a surgical drain?","शल्यक्रियामा drain राख्नुको मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["To close the skin incision","To deliver nutrition","To allow unwanted blood, fluid or air to leave a surgical area when indicated","To replace wound assessment"],2,"A drain allows selected collections of blood, fluid or air to exit and may help monitor postoperative drainage.","आवश्यक अवस्थामा शल्यक्रियास्थलमा जम्मा हुने रगत, तरल वा हावा बाहिर निकाल्न र drainage निगरानी गर्न drain राखिन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["A soft swelling near a recent incision contains clear, straw-coloured fluid. Which complication is most likely?","भर्खरको चिरा नजिक नरम सुन्निएको भागमा सफा पहेँलो-जस्तो तरल छ भने सम्भावित समस्या के हो?",["Arterial thrombosis","Wound dehiscence","Keloid","Seroma"],3,"A seroma is a collection of serous fluid in tissue spaces, often near a surgical wound.","Seroma भनेको शल्यक्रियाको घाउ वरिपरिका तन्तुबीच serous fluid जम्मा हुनु हो।","General Surgery"],
["What does surgical debridement involve?","Surgical debridement भन्नाले के गरिन्छ?",["Removal of dead, damaged or infected tissue to support wound management","Closing a wound without cleaning it","Applying a tight cast to a limb","Draining the urinary bladder"],0,"Debridement removes devitalized or contaminated tissue when clinically indicated and supports wound-bed management.","आवश्यकताअनुसार मरेको, बिग्रिएको वा दूषित तन्तु हटाएर घाउको उचित व्यवस्थापन गर्नुलाई debridement भनिन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["Which appearance is generally expected in a healthy, well-perfused intestinal stoma?","स्वस्थ र राम्रो रक्तसञ्चार भएको intestinal stoma सामान्यतया कस्तो देखिन्छ?",["Dry, black and hard","Moist and pink to red","Pale grey and cold","Blue with increasing pain"],1,"A healthy stoma is usually moist and pink or red because of its blood supply.","रक्तसञ्चार राम्रो भएको स्वस्थ stoma प्रायः ओसिलो र गुलाबी वा रातो देखिन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["A newly formed stoma becomes dusky purple or black. What is the most appropriate action?","नयाँ बनाइएको stoma गाढा बैजनी वा कालो देखियो भने उपयुक्त कदम के हो?",["Wait several days without review","Cover it tightly with adhesive tape","Arrange urgent surgical assessment because impaired blood supply is possible","Apply a warm compress and discharge the patient"],2,"A dusky, purple or black stoma may indicate compromised blood supply and needs urgent surgical review.","Stoma बैजनी वा कालो हुनुमा रक्तसञ्चार बिग्रिएको हुन सक्छ, त्यसैले तुरुन्त शल्यचिकित्सकीय मूल्याङ्कन आवश्यक हुन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["Why is fluid balance monitoring particularly important in a patient with a high-output ileostomy?","धेरै मात्रामा दिसा-जस्तो पदार्थ निस्कने ileostomy भएका बिरामीमा fluid balance किन महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ?",["It prevents all wound infections","It measures bone healing","It confirms normal vision","Large fluid and electrolyte losses can cause dehydration"],3,"High ileostomy output can cause significant water and electrolyte loss, so intake, output and clinical hydration need monitoring.","Ileostomy बाट धेरै पदार्थ निस्कँदा पानी र electrolytes धेरै गुम्न सक्छ; त्यसैले intake-output र hydration निगरानी गर्नुपर्छ।","General Surgery"],
["Which is a common reason for inserting a nasogastric tube in a patient with bowel obstruction?","आन्द्रा अवरोध भएको बिरामीमा nasogastric tube राख्नुको सामान्य कारण के हो?",["Gastric decompression to reduce vomiting and distension when clinically indicated","To repair the bowel wall","To measure blood glucose","To provide oxygen directly to the lungs"],0,"Nasogastric decompression may relieve gastric contents and reduce vomiting in selected patients with bowel obstruction.","आवश्यक अवस्थामा nasogastric tube ले पेटको सामग्री बाहिर निकालेर बान्ता र पेट फुल्ने समस्या कम गर्न मद्दत गर्छ।","General Surgery"],
["Which finding is most suggestive of an incarcerated hernia?","Incarcerated hernia को सम्भावना देखाउने प्रमुख लक्षण कुन हो?",["A painless swelling that disappears completely on lying down","A previously reducible hernia that can no longer be pushed back","A soft swelling that reduces easily","A healed surgical scar"],1,"An incarcerated hernia is trapped and irreducible; pain, vomiting or tenderness raises concern for obstruction or strangulation.","Incarcerated hernia भित्र अड्किएको र फर्काउन नसकिने हुन्छ; दुखाइ, बान्ता वा tenderness भए आन्द्रा अवरोध वा strangulation को चिन्ता हुन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["Which feature raises concern that a hernia may be strangulated?","Hernia strangulated भएको शंका बढाउने लक्षण कुन हो?",["A longstanding painless reducible swelling","A swelling that disappears while lying down","Severe persistent pain with tenderness and systemic illness","A small painless swelling after coughing"],2,"Severe persistent pain, tenderness and systemic features may indicate compromised blood supply and require emergency surgical assessment.","लगातार कडा दुखाइ, tenderness र शरीरमा गम्भीर असर देखिनुमा hernia को रक्तसञ्चार रोकिएको हुन सक्छ; आकस्मिक शल्यचिकित्सकीय जाँच चाहिन्छ।","General Surgery"],
["Which action is appropriate when a patient is suspected of having an incarcerated or strangulated hernia?","Incarcerated वा strangulated hernia को शंका हुँदा कुन कदम उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Attempt repeated forceful reduction","Give food and fluids before assessment","Apply vigorous massage to the swelling","Arrange urgent surgical assessment and avoid forceful manipulation"],3,"Suspected strangulation is an emergency; avoid forceful manipulation and arrange urgent surgical assessment.","Strangulation को शंका आकस्मिक अवस्था हो; जबर्जस्ती भित्र धकेल्ने वा मिच्ने नगरी तुरुन्त शल्यचिकित्सकीय मूल्याङ्कन गराउनुहोस्।","General Surgery"]
]);

