 // Additional Clinical Pathology questions: source-linked, bilingual, pending independent expert review.
 practiceQ.push(
 ["What does an increased reticulocyte count usually indicate?","Reticulocyte count बढ्नुले सामान्यतया के संकेत गर्छ?",["Increased red-cell production by the bone marrow","Complete absence of red-cell production","Reduced platelet production only","A definite bacterial infection"],0,"Reticulocytes are immature red blood cells. An increased count commonly reflects a marrow response to blood loss or haemolysis; interpret with the clinical picture and haemoglobin.","Reticulocyte अपरिपक्व रातो रक्तकोष हुन्। यसको संख्या बढ्नुले रक्तस्राव वा haemolysis पछि bone marrow ले नयाँ RBC बनाइरहेको संकेत गर्न सक्छ; clinical अवस्थासँगै व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्।","Clinical Pathology",["Merck Manual: Evaluation of anemia","https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/hematology-and-oncology/anemias/approach-to-the-patient-with-anemia",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["A blood sample for potassium is visibly haemolysed. What is the main concern?","Potassium जाँचका लागि लिइएको रगतको नमुना haemolysed देखिन्छ। मुख्य चिन्ता के हो?",["Potassium may be falsely elevated","Potassium is always falsely low","Haemolysis confirms kidney failure","The sample becomes suitable for culture"],0,"Haemolysis can release intracellular potassium and cause a falsely high result. Follow laboratory policy for rejection or recollection.","Haemolysis हुँदा कोषभित्रको potassium बाहिर निस्केर नतिजा झूटो रूपमा बढ्न सक्छ। प्रयोगशालाको नियमअनुसार नमुना अस्वीकार वा पुनः संकलन गर्नुहोस्।","Clinical Pathology",["MedlinePlus: Potassium blood test","https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/potassium-blood-test/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which urine sample is generally preferred for routine bacterial culture in a non-catheterized adult?","Catheter नभएको वयस्कमा सामान्य bacterial urine culture का लागि कुन नमुना प्राथमिक हुन्छ?",["Midstream clean-catch urine","Urine collected from the toilet bowl","First drops without cleaning","A sample left at room temperature overnight"],0,"A properly collected midstream clean-catch specimen reduces contamination. Transport promptly or preserve according to laboratory instructions.","सही तरिकाले संकलन गरिएको midstream clean-catch पिसाबले contamination घटाउँछ। प्रयोगशालाको निर्देशनअनुसार छिटो पठाउनुहोस् वा सुरक्षित राख्नुहोस्।","Clinical Pathology",["MedlinePlus: Urine culture","https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/urine-culture/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["What is the primary purpose of a peripheral blood smear?","Peripheral blood smear को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["To examine blood-cell morphology","To measure blood pressure","To determine urine output","To identify all viruses directly"],0,"A peripheral smear allows microscopic assessment of red-cell, white-cell and platelet morphology and may support further investigation.","Peripheral smear ले microscope बाट RBC, WBC र platelet को आकार तथा बनावट हेर्न मद्दत गर्छ र थप जाँचको आधार दिन सक्छ।","Clinical Pathology",["Merck Manual: Approach to the patient with anemia","https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/hematology-and-oncology/anemias/approach-to-the-patient-with-anemia",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["A laboratory receives an unlabeled blood specimen. What should staff do?","प्रयोगशालामा नाम/पहिचान नभएको रगतको नमुना आएमा के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Reject or manage strictly under the laboratory's specimen-identification policy","Guess the patient's identity from the request form","Label it using the next patient's details","Process it urgently without documentation"],0,"An unlabeled specimen cannot be reliably linked to a patient. Follow the laboratory rejection and recollection policy; never guess or relabel from assumption.","पहिचान नभएको नमुना बिरामीसँग विश्वसनीय रूपमा जोड्न सकिँदैन। प्रयोगशालाको rejection र पुनः संकलन नीति पालना गर्नुहोस्; अनुमानका आधारमा label नलगाउनुहोस्।","Clinical Pathology",["WHO: Laboratory quality management system handbook","https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789241548274",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
 ["Which result is most directly used to assess the blood's oxygen-carrying protein concentration?","रगतको अक्सिजन बोक्ने प्रोटिनको मात्रा जाँच्न कुन नतिजा प्रत्यक्ष प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Haemoglobin concentration","Serum sodium","Platelet count","ESR"],0,"Haemoglobin concentration estimates the amount of oxygen-carrying haemoglobin in blood; interpret using age, sex, pregnancy status and local reference ranges.","Haemoglobin concentration ले रगतमा अक्सिजन बोक्ने haemoglobin को मात्रा देखाउँछ; उमेर, लिङ्ग, गर्भावस्था र स्थानीय reference range अनुसार व्याख्या गर्नुहोस्।","Clinical Pathology",["WHO: Haemoglobin concentrations for the diagnosis of anaemia","https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240000124",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which test is commonly used to monitor long-term average blood glucose?","लामो अवधिको औसत रगतको glucose निगरानी गर्न कुन परीक्षण प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["HbA1c","Serum amylase","Bleeding time","ESR"],0,"HbA1c reflects average glycaemia over roughly the preceding 2–3 months, but conditions affecting red-cell lifespan can alter interpretation.","HbA1c ले करिब पछिल्ला २–३ महिनाको औसत glucose अवस्था देखाउँछ; RBC को आयु बदल्ने अवस्थाले नतिजा प्रभावित गर्न सक्छ।","Clinical Pathology",["NIDDK: The A1C test & diabetes","https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diagnostic-tests/a1c-test",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which blood component is primarily responsible for clot formation through platelet plug formation?","Platelet plug बनाएर clot बन्न सुरु गर्न मुख्य भूमिका कसको हुन्छ?",["Platelets","Red blood cells","Albumin","Neutrophils"],0,"Platelets adhere and aggregate at an injured vessel to form the initial platelet plug; coagulation factors then reinforce the clot with fibrin.","रक्तनलीमा चोट लाग्दा platelet टाँसिएर र जम्मा भएर प्रारम्भिक plug बनाउँछन्; coagulation factors ले fibrin बनाएर clot बलियो बनाउँछन्।","Clinical Pathology",["Merck Manual: Overview of platelet disorders","https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/hematology-and-oncology/thrombocytopenia-and-platelet-dysfunction/overview-of-platelet-disorders",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["What is the safest action when a blood-culture bottle is contaminated during collection?","रगतको culture संकलन गर्दा bottle वा नमुना दूषित भएमा सुरक्षित कदम के हो?",["Document and follow protocol for recollection with proper aseptic technique","Report it as a confirmed bloodstream infection","Add disinfectant into the bottle","Hide the collection problem"],0,"Collection contamination can cause misleading positive cultures. Document the event and follow local protocol for repeat collection using aseptic technique.","संकलनको contamination ले गलत positive culture आउन सक्छ। घटना अभिलेख गर्नुहोस् र aseptic technique प्रयोग गरी पुनः संकलन गर्ने स्थानीय protocol पालना गर्नुहोस्।","Clinical Pathology",["CDC: Blood culture contamination","https://www.cdc.gov/antibiotic-use/hcp/clinical-care/adult-outpatient.html",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which finding is most characteristic of iron-deficiency anaemia on a blood film?","Blood film मा iron-deficiency anaemia सँग बढी मिल्ने विशेषता कुन हो?",["Microcytic, hypochromic red cells","Macrocytes with hypersegmented neutrophils","Spherocytes in every case","Normal red-cell size with high haemoglobin"],0,"Iron deficiency commonly produces microcytic, hypochromic red cells. Confirm and investigate the cause using appropriate clinical and laboratory assessment.","Iron कमी हुँदा प्रायः साना र फिक्का RBC (microcytic, hypochromic) देखिन्छन्। उपयुक्त clinical तथा laboratory जाँचबाट पुष्टि गरी कारण खोज्नुहोस्।","Clinical Pathology",["Merck Manual: Iron deficiency anemia","https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/hematology-and-oncology/anemias/iron-deficiency-anemia",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );

 // Additional Anatomy & Physiology questions: bilingual, source-linked and pending independent expert review.
 practiceQ.push(
 ["Which part of the brainstem contains vital centres regulating respiration and heart rate?","श्वासप्रश्वास र मुटुको गति नियमन गर्ने vital centres brainstem को कुन भागमा हुन्छन्?",["Medulla oblongata","Cerebellum","Cerebral cortex","Corpus callosum"],0,"The medulla oblongata contains important autonomic centres involved in respiratory and cardiovascular regulation.","Medulla oblongata मा श्वासप्रश्वास र मुटुसम्बन्धी स्वचालित नियमन गर्ने महत्त्वपूर्ण केन्द्र हुन्छन्।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Neuroanatomy, Medulla Oblongata","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK545્યો/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which structure prevents food from entering the trachea during swallowing?","निल्दा खाना trachea मा पस्नबाट कुन संरचनाले रोक्छ?",["Epiglottis","Uvula","Thyroid cartilage","Vocal ligament"],0,"The epiglottis helps cover the laryngeal inlet during swallowing, reducing entry of food or liquid into the airway.","निल्ने क्रममा epiglottis ले larynx को प्रवेशद्वार ढाक्न मद्दत गर्छ र खाना/तरल airway मा पस्ने जोखिम घटाउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: The Respiratory System","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/22-introduction",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which hormone increases blood calcium concentration?","रगतमा calcium को मात्रा बढाउने hormone कुन हो?",["Parathyroid hormone (PTH)","Calcitonin","Insulin","Aldosterone"],0,"Parathyroid hormone raises blood calcium through effects on bone, kidneys and vitamin D activation.","Parathyroid hormone ले हड्डी, मिर्गौला र vitamin D सक्रियतामार्फत रगतको calcium बढाउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NIDDK: Parathyroid glands","https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/endocrine-diseases/primary-hyperparathyroidism",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Where does most nutrient absorption occur in the digestive tract?","पाचन प्रणालीमा धेरैजसो पोषक तत्त्व कहाँ अवशोषित हुन्छन्?",["Small intestine","Stomach","Large intestine","Oesophagus"],0,"Most digestion and nutrient absorption occur in the small intestine, aided by its folds, villi and microvilli.","सानो आन्द्राका folds, villi र microvilli को सहयोगले धेरैजसो पाचन र पोषक तत्त्वको अवशोषण हुन्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NIDDK: Your digestive system & how it works","https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/digestive-diseases/digestive-system-how-it-works",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which blood vessel carries deoxygenated blood from the heart to the lungs?","मुटुबाट अक्सिजन कम भएको रगत फोक्सोमा लैजाने रक्तनली कुन हो?",["Pulmonary artery","Pulmonary vein","Aorta","Coronary artery"],0,"The pulmonary arteries carry deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs for gas exchange.","Pulmonary artery ले right ventricle बाट अक्सिजन कम भएको रगत ग्यास आदानप्रदानका लागि फोक्सोमा लैजान्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: Blood flow through the heart","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/19-3-cardiac-cycle",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
 ["Which part of the nephron is primarily responsible for the greatest proportion of filtered water and solute reabsorption?","Nephron को कुन भागमा छानिएको पानी र solute को सबैभन्दा ठूलो अंश पुनःअवशोषण हुन्छ?",["Proximal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct","Distal convoluted tubule","Bowman's capsule"],0,"The proximal convoluted tubule reabsorbs the largest share of filtered sodium, water, glucose, amino acids and other solutes.","Proximal convoluted tubule ले छानिएको sodium, पानी, glucose, amino acids लगायतका धेरैजसो पदार्थ पुनःअवशोषण गर्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Renal Physiology","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK538339/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which cranial nerve is responsible for the sense of smell?","सुँघ्ने क्षमताका लागि कुन cranial nerve जिम्मेवार हुन्छ?",["Olfactory nerve (I)","Optic nerve (II)","Trigeminal nerve (V)","Facial nerve (VII)"],0,"The olfactory nerve, cranial nerve I, carries sensory information for smell from the nasal olfactory epithelium.","Olfactory nerve अर्थात् cranial nerve I ले नाकको olfactory epithelium बाट गन्धसम्बन्धी सूचना मस्तिष्कमा पुर्‍याउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Neuroanatomy, Cranial Nerves","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK11104/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which cells produce myelin in the central nervous system?","Central nervous system मा myelin बनाउने कोषिका कुन हुन्?",["Oligodendrocytes","Schwann cells","Astrocytes","Microglia"],0,"Oligodendrocytes form myelin around axons in the central nervous system; Schwann cells perform this role in the peripheral nervous system.","Oligodendrocytes ले central nervous system का axon वरिपरि myelin बनाउँछन्; peripheral nervous system मा यो काम Schwann cells ले गर्छन्।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Neuroanatomy, Glial Cells","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK10869/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which chamber receives oxygenated blood returning from the lungs?","फोक्सोबाट फर्किएको oxygenated blood मुटुको कुन कोठामा आउँछ?",["Left atrium","Right atrium","Left ventricle","Right ventricle"],0,"Pulmonary veins return oxygenated blood from the lungs to the left atrium.","Pulmonary veins ले फोक्सोबाट oxygenated blood लाई left atrium मा ल्याउँछन्।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: Blood flow through the heart","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/19-3-cardiac-cycle",false,"2026-11-25"]],
 ["Which type of muscle is found in the wall of the intestine?","आन्द्राको भित्तामा कुन प्रकारको मांसपेशी पाइन्छ?",["Smooth muscle","Skeletal muscle","Cardiac muscle","Voluntary striated muscle"],0,"The intestinal wall contains smooth muscle that contracts involuntarily to move contents through peristalsis.","आन्द्राको भित्तामा रहेको smooth muscle अनैच्छिक रूपमा खुम्चिएर peristalsis मार्फत पदार्थ अघि बढाउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: The Digestive System","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/23-introduction",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );

 // Pharmacology & Pharmacy: additional bilingual practice and mock questions (pending expert review)
 practiceQ.push(
  ["Which route of administration provides the fastest systemic effect in an emergency?","आपत्कालीन अवस्थामा कुन administration route ले सबैभन्दा छिटो systemic effect दिन्छ?",["Intravenous","Oral","Topical","Rectal"],0,"Intravenous administration delivers a medicine directly into the bloodstream and generally provides the fastest systemic effect.","Intravenous route ले औषधि सिधै रगतमा पुर्‍याउँछ, त्यसैले सामान्यतया छिटो systemic effect दिन्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["NCBI Bookshelf: Drug Administration Routes","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557744/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["What is the main purpose of a loading dose?","Loading dose दिनुको मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["To reach the target drug concentration rapidly","To prevent all adverse effects","To reduce the medicine's absorption","To replace every maintenance dose"],0,"A loading dose helps achieve the desired therapeutic concentration more rapidly than starting with maintenance dosing alone.","Loading dose ले maintenance dose मात्र सुरु गर्नुभन्दा छिटो आवश्यक therapeutic concentration प्राप्त गर्न मद्दत गर्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["NCBI Bookshelf: Pharmacokinetics","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557744/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which term describes an unwanted harmful response to a medicine at a normal dose?","सामान्य dose मा औषधि प्रयोग गर्दा हुने अनिच्छित हानिकारक प्रतिक्रियालाई के भनिन्छ?",["Adverse drug reaction","Therapeutic effect","Placebo effect","Drug tolerance"],0,"An adverse drug reaction is a harmful, unintended response occurring with a medicine used at normally prescribed doses.","सामान्य रूपमा निर्धारित dose मा औषधि प्रयोग गर्दा हुने हानिकारक र अनिच्छित प्रतिक्रियालाई adverse drug reaction भनिन्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["WHO: Medication Safety","https://www.who.int/initiatives/medication-without-harm",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which instruction is most important when counselling a patient prescribed an antibiotic?","Antibiotic दिइएको बिरामीलाई परामर्श गर्दा कुन निर्देशन सबैभन्दा महत्वपूर्ण हुन्छ?",["Use it exactly as prescribed and do not share it","Stop it as soon as symptoms improve without advice","Save leftover doses for another illness","Double the next dose after a missed dose"],0,"Patients should take antibiotics exactly as prescribed, avoid sharing them, and seek advice if they have concerns or miss doses.","Antibiotic चिकित्सकले भनेअनुसार लिनुपर्छ, अरूलाई बाँड्नु हुँदैन, र समस्या वा dose छुटेमा स्वास्थ्यकर्मीसँग सल्लाह लिनुपर्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["WHO: Antimicrobial resistance","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/antimicrobial-resistance",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which medicine is commonly used as an antidote for paracetamol overdose?","Paracetamol overdose मा सामान्यतया कुन औषधि antidote का रूपमा प्रयोग गरिन्छ?",["N-acetylcysteine","Atropine","Naloxone","Vitamin K"],0,"N-acetylcysteine replenishes glutathione and helps prevent or reduce liver injury after paracetamol overdose; urgent assessment is essential.","N-acetylcysteine ले glutathione पुनःपूर्ति गरी paracetamol overdose पछि कलेजोमा हुने क्षति रोक्न वा घटाउन मद्दत गर्छ; तुरुन्त स्वास्थ्य मूल्याङ्कन आवश्यक हुन्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["NCBI Bookshelf: Acetaminophen Toxicity","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK441917/",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
  ["Which factor most directly affects the maintenance dose rate for a medicine?","औषधिको maintenance dose rate लाई कुन कुराले प्रत्यक्ष रूपमा बढी प्रभाव पार्छ?",["Drug clearance","Tablet colour","Patient's handwriting","Medicine packaging size"],0,"Maintenance dosing rate is strongly influenced by clearance, which describes how efficiently the body eliminates a drug.","Maintenance dose rate मा clearance को ठूलो प्रभाव हुन्छ; यसले शरीरले औषधि कति प्रभावकारी रूपमा हटाउँछ भन्ने जनाउँछ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["NCBI Bookshelf: Pharmacokinetics","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557744/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["A patient develops wheezing, facial swelling and hypotension soon after an injection. Which medicine is first-line treatment for anaphylaxis?","Injection लगाएपछि बिरामीलाई wheezing, अनुहार सुन्निने र hypotension भयो। Anaphylaxis को first-line उपचार कुन औषधि हो?",["Intramuscular adrenaline (epinephrine)","Oral antihistamine alone","Paracetamol","Aspirin"],0,"Intramuscular adrenaline into the anterolateral thigh is first-line treatment for anaphylaxis; emergency support and monitoring are also required.","Anaphylaxis मा तिघ्राको अगाडिको-बाहिरी भागमा intramuscular adrenaline first-line उपचार हो; आपत्कालीन सहयोग र monitoring पनि आवश्यक हुन्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["Resuscitation Council UK: Emergency treatment of anaphylaxis","https://www.resus.org.uk/library/additional-guidance/guidance-anaphylaxis/emergency-treatment",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which electrolyte disturbance is a recognised risk of loop diuretics such as furosemide?","Furosemide जस्ता loop diuretics ले कुन electrolyte समस्या गराउन सक्छन्?",["Hypokalaemia","Hypercalcaemia in every patient","Hypernatraemia in every patient","Hypermagnesaemia"],0,"Loop diuretics increase urinary potassium loss and can cause hypokalaemia; electrolyte monitoring may be needed.","Loop diuretics ले पिसाबबाट potassium को हानि बढाउन सक्छन् र hypokalaemia गराउन सक्छन्; electrolyte monitoring आवश्यक पर्न सक्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["NCBI Bookshelf: Loop Diuretics","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK546656/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["What should be checked first when a medicine dose appears unusually high on a prescription?","Prescription मा औषधिको dose असामान्य रूपमा धेरै देखिएमा पहिले के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Verify the prescription with the prescriber before administration","Give it immediately","Reduce it independently without documentation","Ask another patient"],0,"An unclear or potentially unsafe prescription should be clarified with the prescriber before the medicine is administered.","अस्पष्ट वा असुरक्षित हुन सक्ने prescription औषधि दिनुअघि prescriber सँग पुष्टि गर्नुपर्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["WHO: Medication Without Harm","https://www.who.int/initiatives/medication-without-harm",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which statement about insulin storage is generally correct for unopened insulin?","नखोलिएको insulin को storage सम्बन्धमा सामान्यतया कुन भनाइ सही हो?",["Store refrigerated according to the product instructions; do not freeze","Keep it in direct sunlight","Always store it in a freezer","Leave it in a hot vehicle"],0,"Unopened insulin is generally stored in a refrigerator within the manufacturer's specified temperature range and must not be frozen; product-specific instructions should be followed.","नखोलिएको insulin सामान्यतया उत्पादकले तोकेको तापक्रम सीमाभित्र refrigerator मा राखिन्छ र freeze गर्नु हुँदैन; सम्बन्धित उत्पादनको निर्देशन पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Pharmacology & Pharmacy",["FDA: Insulin storage and handling information","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/special-features/insulin-storage-and-syringe-safety",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 
 // General Surgery: additional bilingual practice and mock questions (pending expert review)
 practiceQ.push(
  ["What is the first priority when assessing a patient with major trauma?","गम्भीर चोट लागेको बिरामीको मूल्याङ्कन गर्दा पहिलो प्राथमिकता के हो?",["Airway with cervical spine protection","Detailed wound dressing","Taking a full dietary history","Measuring height"],0,"Use the ABCDE approach. Assess and secure the airway while protecting the cervical spine when trauma is suspected.","ABCDE विधि अपनाउनुहोस्। चोटको शंका हुँदा cervical spine सुरक्षित राख्दै airway जाँचेर सुरक्षित गर्नु पहिलो प्राथमिकता हो।","General Surgery",["NICE: Major trauma assessment and initial management","https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng39",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which finding is most suggestive of wound infection after surgery?","शल्यक्रियापछि घाउमा संक्रमण भएको संकेत कुन हो?",["Increasing redness, warmth, pain and purulent discharge","A clean, dry wound with improving pain","A small stable bruise only","Mild itching without other symptoms"],0,"Increasing redness, warmth, pain and pus are concerning features of a surgical-site infection and require clinical assessment.","रातोपन, तातोपन, दुखाइ बढ्नु र पीप आउनु surgical-site infection का शंकास्पद लक्षण हुन् र चिकित्सकीय जाँच आवश्यक हुन्छ।","General Surgery",["CDC: Surgical Site Infection","https://www.cdc.gov/surgical-site-infections/about/index.html",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["What is the immediate first-aid action for severe external bleeding?","धेरै रगत बगिरहेको अवस्थामा तत्काल प्राथमिक उपचार के हो?",["Apply firm direct pressure to the wound","Wash repeatedly without pressure","Give oral fluids first","Remove any deeply embedded object"],0,"Apply firm direct pressure using a dressing or clean cloth. For life-threatening limb bleeding, use a tourniquet if trained and indicated; arrange emergency care.","ड्रेसिङ वा सफा कपडाले घाउमा बलियो प्रत्यक्ष दबाब दिनुहोस्। हातखुट्टाबाट ज्यान जोखिम हुने रक्तस्रावमा तालिम प्राप्त व्यक्तिले आवश्यकताअनुसार tourniquet प्रयोग गरी आपत्कालीन उपचार मिलाउनुपर्छ।","General Surgery",["NHS: Severe bleeding first aid","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/first-aid/bleeding/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which clinical feature is typical of acute appendicitis?","Acute appendicitis मा सामान्यतया कुन लक्षण देखिन्छ?",["Pain migrating from around the umbilicus to the right lower abdomen","Painless jaundice","Pain only in the left shoulder","Chronic painless swelling of both legs"],0,"Acute appendicitis classically causes abdominal pain that may begin near the umbilicus and later localise to the right lower quadrant, often with nausea or fever.","Acute appendicitis मा सुरुमा नाइटो वरिपरि दुखाइ भएर पछि दायाँ तल्लो पेटतिर सर्न सक्छ; वाकवाकी वा ज्वरो पनि हुन सक्छ।","General Surgery",["NIDDK: Appendicitis","https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/digestive-diseases/appendicitis",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["What should be done first for a suspected fracture before transport?","हड्डी भाँचिएको शंका हुँदा बिरामीलाई लैजानुअघि पहिले के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Immobilise the injured part in the position found","Attempt to straighten the limb forcefully","Massage the fracture site","Ask the patient to walk"],0,"Immobilise the injured part and the joints above and below when possible; check circulation and sensation, and arrange appropriate medical care.","चोट लागेको भागलाई सम्भव भए माथि र तलका जोर्नीसहित स्थिर राख्नुहोस्; रक्तसञ्चार र संवेदना जाँचेर उचित उपचारको व्यवस्था गर्नुहोस्।","General Surgery",["NHS: Broken arm or wrist","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/broken-arm-or-wrist/",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
  ["A patient with a painful, irreducible groin swelling and vomiting may have which emergency?","दुख्ने, भित्र नधसिने groin swelling र बान्ता भएको बिरामीमा कुन आपत्कालीन अवस्था हुन सक्छ?",["Strangulated hernia","Simple reducible hernia","Lipoma","Varicose vein"],0,"A painful irreducible hernia with vomiting may indicate strangulation or bowel obstruction and needs urgent surgical assessment.","दुख्ने र भित्र नधसिने hernia सँग बान्ता हुनु strangulation वा bowel obstruction को संकेत हुन सक्छ; तुरुन्त शल्यचिकित्सकीय मूल्याङ्कन आवश्यक हुन्छ।","General Surgery",["NHS: Hernia","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/hernia/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which combination is most concerning for acute compartment syndrome?","Acute compartment syndrome को सबैभन्दा शंकास्पद लक्षणहरूको संयोजन कुन हो?",["Severe pain out of proportion and pain on passive stretch","Mild bruising with no pain","Itching relieved by scratching","A painless superficial abrasion"],0,"Severe pain disproportionate to the injury, especially pain on passive stretch, is an important early warning sign; urgent surgical assessment is required.","चोटको तुलनामा अत्यधिक दुखाइ, विशेषगरी अंग तन्काउँदा हुने दुखाइ, प्रारम्भिक महत्वपूर्ण चेतावनी हो; तुरुन्त शल्यचिकित्सकीय जाँच चाहिन्छ।","General Surgery",["AAOS: Compartment Syndrome","https://orthoinfo.aaos.org/en/diseases--conditions/compartment-syndrome/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["A trauma patient has sudden severe breathlessness, hypotension and absent breath sounds on one side. What should be suspected?","चोट लागेको बिरामीलाई अचानक सास फेर्न गाह्रो, hypotension र एकातिर श्वासध्वनि नआएमा के शंका गर्नुपर्छ?",["Tension pneumothorax","Simple ankle sprain","Acute otitis media","Renal colic"],0,"Tension pneumothorax is a life-threatening emergency. Clinical suspicion requires immediate emergency treatment by a trained clinician; do not delay for imaging.","Tension pneumothorax ज्यान जोखिमको आपत्कालीन अवस्था हो। शंका भए तालिम प्राप्त चिकित्सकले तुरुन्त उपचार गर्नुपर्छ; imaging पर्खेर ढिलाइ गर्नु हुँदैन।","General Surgery",["NICE: Major trauma assessment and initial management","https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng39",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which symptom pattern is typical of mechanical intestinal obstruction?","Mechanical intestinal obstruction मा सामान्यतया कुन लक्षणहरूको समूह देखिन्छ?",["Colicky abdominal pain, vomiting, distension and inability to pass stool or flatus","Painless jaundice alone","Isolated headache and blurred vision","Frequent urination without abdominal symptoms"],0,"Mechanical bowel obstruction commonly presents with colicky abdominal pain, vomiting, abdominal distension and reduced or absent passage of stool and flatus.","Mechanical bowel obstruction मा पेट बटारिने दुखाइ, बान्ता, पेट फुल्ने र दिसा वा ग्यास ननिस्कने लक्षण देखिन सक्छन्।","General Surgery",["NIDDK: Intestinal obstruction","https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/digestive-diseases/intestinal-obstruction",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["After major surgery, unilateral calf swelling and tenderness should raise concern for what condition?","ठूलो शल्यक्रियापछि एउटा पिँडुला सुन्निने र दुख्ने भए कुन अवस्थाको शंका गर्नुपर्छ?",["Deep vein thrombosis","Migraine","Appendicitis","Otitis externa"],0,"Unilateral calf swelling and tenderness can indicate deep vein thrombosis. Prompt clinical assessment is needed because a clot can travel to the lungs.","एउटा पिँडुला सुन्निनु र दुख्नु deep vein thrombosis को संकेत हुन सक्छ। रगतको clot फोक्सोमा पुग्न सक्ने भएकाले छिटो चिकित्सकीय जाँच आवश्यक हुन्छ।","General Surgery",["NHS: Deep vein thrombosis","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/deep-vein-thrombosis-dvt/",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );

 // Community Health: additional bilingual practice and mock questions (pending expert review)
 practiceQ.push(
  ["Which indicator measures the number of new cases of a disease occurring in a population during a specified period?","निर्धारित अवधिमा जनसंख्यामा रोगका नयाँ केस कति भए भनेर कुन सूचकले मापन गर्छ?",["Incidence","Prevalence","Case fatality rate","Crude birth rate"],0,"Incidence measures new cases arising in a population at risk during a specified time period.","Incidence ले निश्चित अवधिमा जोखिममा रहेको जनसंख्यामा देखिएका नयाँ रोगीको संख्या वा दर मापन गर्छ।","Community Health",["CDC: Principles of Epidemiology","https://www.cdc.gov/csels/dsepd/ss1978/lesson3/section2.html",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["What is the main purpose of contact tracing during an infectious disease outbreak?","संक्रामक रोगको प्रकोपमा contact tracing गर्नुको मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["Identify and follow people exposed to an infected person","Treat every person with antibiotics","Replace laboratory confirmation in all cases","Stop routine immunisation"],0,"Contact tracing identifies people who may have been exposed so they can receive guidance, testing or monitoring and help reduce further transmission.","Contact tracing ले संक्रमित व्यक्तिको सम्पर्कमा आएका मानिस पहिचान गर्छ, ताकि उनीहरूलाई आवश्यक सल्लाह, परीक्षण वा निगरानी दिन र संक्रमण फैलिन कम गर्न सकियोस्।","Community Health",["WHO: Contact tracing","https://www.who.int/health-topics/contact-tracing",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which measure is most appropriate for preventing diarrhoeal diseases at household level?","घरपरिवारमा झाडापखाला रोक्न सबैभन्दा उपयुक्त उपाय कुन हो?",["Safe drinking water, sanitation and handwashing","Taking antibiotics every week","Avoiding all fruits","Using antibiotics to purify water"],0,"Safe water, sanitation and handwashing with soap are core measures for preventing diarrhoeal disease transmission.","सुरक्षित पानी, सरसफाइ र साबुनपानीले हात धुनु झाडापखाला फैलिन रोक्ने मुख्य उपाय हुन्।","Community Health",["WHO: Diarrhoeal disease","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/diarrhoeal-disease",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["In a screening programme, what does a highly sensitive test help to minimise?","Screening कार्यक्रममा उच्च sensitivity भएको परीक्षणले कुन कुरा कम गर्न मद्दत गर्छ?",["False-negative results","False-positive results","The need for consent","Disease prevalence"],0,"A highly sensitive test detects most people who have the condition and therefore helps reduce false-negative results.","उच्च sensitivity भएको परीक्षणले रोग भएका धेरैजसो व्यक्तिलाई पहिचान गर्छ र false-negative नतिजा कम गर्न मद्दत गर्छ।","Community Health",["CDC: Principles of Epidemiology – Screening","https://www.cdc.gov/csels/dsepd/ss1978/lesson3/section6.html",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["What is the best immediate public-health action when a suspected foodborne outbreak is reported?","खानाबाट सर्ने रोगको प्रकोप भएको शंका रिपोर्ट हुँदा जनस्वास्थ्यको पहिलो उपयुक्त कदम के हो?",["Notify the responsible public-health authority and begin investigation","Wait until many more people become ill","Destroy all food records","Give antibiotics to every exposed person"],0,"Prompt notification and coordinated investigation help identify the source, limit exposure and guide control measures.","तुरुन्त सम्बन्धित जनस्वास्थ्य निकायलाई जानकारी दिई समन्वित अनुसन्धान सुरु गर्दा स्रोत पहिचान, थप exposure रोकथाम र नियन्त्रणका उपाय तय गर्न मद्दत हुन्छ।","Community Health",["WHO: Foodborne diseases","https://www.who.int/health-topics/foodborne-diseases",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
  ["A community reports 20 new cases of a disease among 1,000 people at risk over one month. What is the cumulative incidence for that month?","एक महिनामा जोखिममा रहेका १,००० जनामध्ये रोगका २० नयाँ केस देखिए। त्यस महिनाको cumulative incidence कति हो?",["2%","0.2%","20%","50%"],0,"Cumulative incidence is 20 divided by 1,000, multiplied by 100: 2% for the stated period, assuming the denominator is the population at risk at the start.","Cumulative incidence = २० ÷ १,००० × १०० = २% हुन्छ। यो अवधिको सुरुवातमा जोखिममा रहेको जनसंख्या denominator भएको मानिएको छ।","Community Health",["CDC: Principles of Epidemiology","https://www.cdc.gov/csels/dsepd/ss1978/lesson3/section2.html",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which vaccine type is generally more affected by freezing and must be protected from it?","कुन प्रकारका खोपहरू सामान्यतया जम्ने तापक्रमबाट बढी प्रभावित हुन्छन् र freeze हुनबाट जोगाउनुपर्छ?",["Adsorbed vaccines such as DPT and hepatitis B","All oral vaccines equally","Every vaccine is freeze-proof","Only vaccines supplied as tablets"],0,"Many adsorbed vaccines, including DPT-containing and hepatitis B vaccines, are freeze-sensitive. Follow the national immunisation programme and product guidance.","DPT-containing र hepatitis B जस्ता धेरै adsorbed vaccines जम्ने तापक्रमप्रति संवेदनशील हुन्छन्। राष्ट्रिय खोप कार्यक्रम र उत्पादनको निर्देशन पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Community Health",["WHO: Vaccine management and cold chain","https://www.who.int/teams/immunization-vaccines-and-biologicals/essential-programme-on-immunization/supply-chain",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which epidemiological measure describes the proportion of people with a disease who die from it?","रोग लागेका व्यक्तिमध्ये त्यसै रोगका कारण मृत्यु हुने अनुपातलाई कुन epidemiological measure भनिन्छ?",["Case fatality proportion","Incidence rate","Prevalence","Attack rate of exposure"],0,"The case fatality proportion is the number of deaths among identified cases divided by the total identified cases, expressed as a percentage.","Case fatality proportion भनेको पहिचान भएका केसहरूमध्ये मृत्यु भएका व्यक्तिको अनुपात हो, सामान्यतया प्रतिशतमा व्यक्त गरिन्छ।","Community Health",["CDC: Principles of Epidemiology","https://www.cdc.gov/csels/dsepd/ss1978/lesson3/section3.html",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which study design is especially useful for investigating a rare disease?","दुर्लभ रोगको अनुसन्धान गर्न कुन अध्ययन डिजाइन विशेष उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["Case-control study","Cross-sectional survey only","Ecological study only","Community trial"],0,"A case-control study starts with people who have the disease and suitable controls, then compares prior exposures; it is efficient for rare diseases.","Case-control study मा रोग भएका व्यक्तिहरू र उपयुक्त control समूह लिएर पहिलेका exposure तुलना गरिन्छ; दुर्लभ रोगमा यो उपयोगी हुन्छ।","Community Health",["CDC: Principles of Epidemiology – Study designs","https://www.cdc.gov/csels/dsepd/ss1978/lesson1/section7.html",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which action is most appropriate after a needle-stick injury in a health worker?","स्वास्थ्यकर्मीलाई सुईले घोचेपछि सबैभन्दा उपयुक्त कदम के हो?",["Wash the area promptly, report immediately and seek risk assessment","Squeeze the wound aggressively and ignore it","Apply bleach to the puncture","Wait for symptoms before reporting"],0,"Wash the site with soap and water, report promptly, and obtain urgent occupational-health assessment for exposure management and possible post-exposure prophylaxis.","घाउलाई साबुनपानीले तुरुन्त धुनुहोस्, घटना रिपोर्ट गर्नुहोस् र exposure management तथा आवश्यक post-exposure prophylaxis का लागि तत्काल occupational-health मूल्याङ्कन लिनुहोस्।","Community Health",["CDC: Responding to HBV exposures in health care settings","https://www.cdc.gov/hepatitis-b/hcp/infection-control/index.html",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );

 // General Medicine: additional bilingual practice and mock questions (pending expert review)
 practiceQ.push(
  ["Which clinical feature is most characteristic of hypoglycaemia?","Hypoglycaemia को सबैभन्दा विशेषता भएको clinical feature कुन हो?",["Sweating, tremor and confusion","Slow hair growth only","Painless jaundice","Bilateral ankle deformity"],0,"Hypoglycaemia can cause sweating, tremor, palpitations, hunger, behavioural change and confusion. Check glucose promptly and treat according to the patient's condition and protocol.","Hypoglycaemia हुँदा पसिना आउने, हात काम्ने, मुटु ढुकढुक हुने, भोक लाग्ने, व्यवहार परिवर्तन र अलमल हुन सक्छ। तुरुन्त glucose जाँच गरी अवस्था र protocol अनुसार उपचार गर्नुपर्छ।","General Medicine",["NHS: Low blood sugar (hypoglycaemia)","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/low-blood-sugar-hypoglycaemia/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which symptom is a warning sign of possible meningitis in an adult?","वयस्कमा meningitis हुन सक्ने चेतावनी संकेत कुन हो?",["Fever with severe headache and neck stiffness","Mild isolated tooth sensitivity","Chronic painless callus","Itchy skin after bathing only"],0,"Fever, severe headache and neck stiffness are important warning features of meningitis; urgent assessment is required, especially with altered consciousness or a non-blanching rash.","ज्वरो, अत्यधिक टाउको दुखाइ र घाँटी कडा हुनु meningitis का महत्वपूर्ण चेतावनी संकेत हुन्। चेतना परिवर्तन वा थिच्दा नहराउने rash भए झन् तुरुन्त जाँच आवश्यक हुन्छ।","General Medicine",["NHS: Meningitis","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/meningitis/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["What is the recommended first response when an adult is having a generalised convulsive seizure?","वयस्कलाई generalized convulsive seizure हुँदा पहिलो उपयुक्त प्रतिक्रिया के हो?",["Protect from injury, cushion the head and time the seizure","Restrain the limbs firmly","Put a spoon or fingers in the mouth","Give water during the convulsion"],0,"Protect the person from nearby hazards, cushion the head, loosen tight clothing and time the seizure. Do not restrain them or put anything in their mouth; seek emergency help when indicated.","व्यक्तिलाई वरपरका वस्तुबाट चोट लाग्न नदिनुहोस्, टाउकोमुनि नरम वस्तु राख्नुहोस् र दौरा कति समय रह्यो टिप्नुहोस्। बलपूर्वक समात्ने वा मुखमा वस्तु हाल्ने नगर्नुहोस्; आवश्यक अवस्थामा आपत्कालीन सहायता बोलाउनुहोस्।","General Medicine",["NHS: What to do if someone has a seizure","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/what-to-do-if-someone-has-a-seizure-fit/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which finding in an adult with asthma suggests a life-threatening attack?","दम भएको वयस्कमा कुन संकेतले ज्यान जोखिमको attack जनाउन सक्छ?",["Silent chest or exhaustion with difficulty speaking","Mild occasional cough with normal speech","Sneezing without breathlessness","Itchy eyes alone"],0,"A silent chest, exhaustion, reduced consciousness or inability to speak in phrases can indicate a life-threatening asthma attack and requires emergency treatment.","Silent chest, अत्यधिक थकान, चेतना घट्नु वा वाक्य बोल्न नसक्नु ज्यान जोखिमको asthma attack का संकेत हुन सक्छन् र आपत्कालीन उपचार चाहिन्छ।","General Medicine",["BTS/SIGN: British guideline on the management of asthma","https://www.brit-thoracic.org.uk/quality-improvement/guidelines/asthma/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which measure is most useful for monitoring long-term glycaemic control in diabetes?","Diabetes मा लामो समयको blood glucose control मूल्याङ्कन गर्न कुन परीक्षण उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["HbA1c","Single random urine colour","Serum sodium alone","White blood cell count"],0,"HbA1c reflects average blood glucose over approximately the previous 2–3 months, although interpretation may be affected by some conditions.","HbA1c ले करिब पछिल्ला २–३ महिनाको औसत blood glucose देखाउँछ; केही अवस्थाले यसको नतिजाको व्याख्यामा असर पार्न सक्छन्।","General Medicine",["CDC: A1C Test for Diabetes","https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/diabetes-testing/prediabetes-a1c-test.html",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
  ["A patient with fever, confusion, rapid breathing and low blood pressure may be developing which life-threatening condition?","ज्वरो, अलमल, छिटो सास र कम रक्तचाप भएको बिरामीमा कुन ज्यान जोखिमको अवस्था विकास भइरहेको हुन सक्छ?",["Sepsis","Stable allergic rhinitis","Simple myopia","Chronic osteoarthritis"],0,"Sepsis is a life-threatening response to infection. Suspected sepsis with organ dysfunction or shock requires urgent recognition, escalation and treatment.","Sepsis संक्रमणप्रति शरीरको ज्यान जोखिमपूर्ण प्रतिक्रिया हो। अंगको कार्य बिग्रिएको वा shock को शंका भए तुरुन्त पहिचान, referral/escalation र उपचार आवश्यक हुन्छ।","General Medicine",["WHO: Sepsis","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/sepsis",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which test is commonly used as an initial screening test for pulmonary tuberculosis in a symptomatic adult where available?","लक्षण भएको वयस्कमा उपलब्ध भए pulmonary tuberculosis को प्रारम्भिक परीक्षणका रूपमा कुन परीक्षण प्रयोग गर्न सकिन्छ?",["Rapid molecular test such as Xpert MTB/RIF","Blood glucose only","ECG only","Urine pregnancy test"],0,"WHO recommends rapid molecular diagnostic tests, such as Xpert MTB/RIF, as initial tests for people with signs and symptoms of TB where available and appropriate.","WHO ले उपलब्ध र उपयुक्त अवस्थामा TB का लक्षण भएका व्यक्तिमा Xpert MTB/RIF जस्ता rapid molecular test लाई प्रारम्भिक परीक्षणका रूपमा सिफारिस गर्छ।","General Medicine",["WHO: WHO consolidated guidelines on tuberculosis","https://www.who.int/teams/global-tuberculosis-programme/diagnosis-treatment",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["A patient suddenly develops facial droop, arm weakness and slurred speech. What is the most appropriate action?","बिरामीको अनुहार एकातिर लत्रियो, हात कमजोर भयो र बोली अस्पष्ट भयो। सबैभन्दा उपयुक्त कदम के हो?",["Treat as suspected stroke and arrange emergency transfer immediately","Allow the patient to sleep and review tomorrow","Give food and water","Massage the weak arm"],0,"Face drooping, arm weakness and speech difficulty are FAST warning signs of stroke. Record the time symptoms began or the patient was last known well and arrange emergency care immediately.","अनुहार लत्रिनु, हात कमजोर हुनु र बोली बिग्रनु stroke का FAST चेतावनी संकेत हुन्। लक्षण सुरु भएको वा अन्तिम पटक सामान्य देखिएको समय टिपेर तुरुन्त आपत्कालीन उपचारको व्यवस्था गर्नुहोस्।","General Medicine",["NHS: Symptoms of a stroke","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/stroke/symptoms/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which finding is a danger sign in a child with acute diarrhoea?","तीव्र झाडापखाला भएको बालबालिकामा कुन संकेत खतरा सूचक हो?",["Unable to drink or drinking poorly with lethargy","Normal activity and drinking well","One formed stool daily","Mild thirst relieved by drinking"],0,"Inability to drink or drinking poorly, lethargy, sunken eyes and very slow skin-pinch return can indicate severe dehydration and require urgent assessment.","पिउन नसक्नु वा निकै कम पिउनु, सुस्त हुनु, आँखा गाडिनु र छाला चिमोट्दा ढिलो फर्किनु गम्भीर dehydration का संकेत हुन सक्छन् र तुरुन्त जाँच चाहिन्छ।","General Medicine",["WHO: Diarrhoeal disease","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/diarrhoeal-disease",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which finding in a patient with dengue should prompt urgent referral for severe dengue assessment?","Dengue भएको बिरामीमा कुन संकेतले severe dengue को लागि तुरुन्त referral आवश्यक बनाउँछ?",["Severe abdominal pain or persistent vomiting","Mild fever alone on the first day","Normal appetite and activity","A small healed scar"],0,"Severe abdominal pain, persistent vomiting, mucosal bleeding, lethargy or restlessness, and fluid accumulation are warning signs that need urgent clinical assessment.","कडा पेट दुखाइ, लगातार बान्ता, mucosal bleeding, अत्यधिक सुस्ती वा बेचैनी र शरीरमा तरल जम्नु dengue का warning signs हुन्; तुरुन्त चिकित्सकीय जाँच आवश्यक हुन्छ।","General Medicine",["WHO: Dengue and severe dengue","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/dengue-and-severe-dengue",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );

 // Anatomy & Physiology: revision MCQs (pending expert review)
 practiceQ.push(
  ["Which part of the heart normally acts as the primary pacemaker?","मुटुको प्राथमिक pacemaker का रूपमा सामान्यतया कुन भागले काम गर्छ?",["Sinoatrial node","Atrioventricular node","Bundle of His","Purkinje fibres"],0,"The sinoatrial (SA) node normally initiates the electrical impulse that sets the heart rhythm.","Sinoatrial (SA) node ले सामान्यतया मुटुको rhythm सुरु गर्ने विद्युतीय impulse उत्पन्न गर्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: Cardiac muscle and electrical activity","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/19-2-cardiac-muscle-and-electrical-activity",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which structure connects the middle ear to the nasopharynx and helps equalise pressure?","Middle ear लाई nasopharynx सँग जोडेर pressure बराबर बनाउन कुन संरचनाले मद्दत गर्छ?",["Auditory (Eustachian) tube","Cochlea","Semicircular canal","Optic nerve"],0,"The auditory tube connects the middle ear to the nasopharynx and helps equalise air pressure across the tympanic membrane.","Auditory tube ले middle ear लाई nasopharynx सँग जोड्छ र tympanic membrane को दुवैतर्फको हावाको pressure बराबर बनाउन मद्दत गर्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: The Ear","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/15-3-the-ear",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which blood vessel carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs?","Right ventricle बाट deoxygenated blood फोक्सोतर्फ लैजाने रक्तनली कुन हो?",["Pulmonary artery","Pulmonary vein","Aorta","Superior vena cava"],0,"The pulmonary trunk leaves the right ventricle and divides into pulmonary arteries that carry deoxygenated blood to the lungs.","Pulmonary trunk right ventricle बाट निस्केर pulmonary arteries मा विभाजित हुन्छ र deoxygenated blood फोक्सोमा लैजान्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: Blood flow through the heart","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/19-3-cardiac-cycle",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which hormone increases blood calcium concentration?","रगतमा calcium को मात्रा बढाउने hormone कुन हो?",["Parathyroid hormone","Calcitonin","Insulin","Aldosterone"],0,"Parathyroid hormone raises blood calcium through effects on bone, kidneys and indirectly intestinal absorption via vitamin D activation.","Parathyroid hormone ले हड्डी, मिर्गौला र vitamin D सक्रियतामार्फत आन्द्राबाट हुने absorption मा प्रभाव पारेर रगतको calcium बढाउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Physiology, Parathyroid Hormone","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK279023/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which part of the brainstem contains vital centres involved in breathing and cardiovascular regulation?","सासप्रश्वास र cardiovascular regulation का महत्वपूर्ण केन्द्र brainstem को कुन भागमा हुन्छन्?",["Medulla oblongata","Cerebellar cortex","Occipital lobe","Corpus callosum"],0,"The medulla oblongata contains important autonomic centres involved in respiratory and cardiovascular regulation.","Medulla oblongata मा सासप्रश्वास र cardiovascular regulation मा संलग्न महत्वपूर्ण autonomic केन्द्रहरू हुन्छन्।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Neuroanatomy, Brainstem","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK545296/",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
  ["Which nephron segment is the main site of glucose reabsorption under normal conditions?","सामान्य अवस्थामा nephron को कुन भागमा glucose को अधिकांश reabsorption हुन्छ?",["Proximal convoluted tubule","Descending limb of loop of Henle","Distal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct"],0,"Filtered glucose is normally reabsorbed predominantly in the proximal convoluted tubule through sodium-glucose transporters.","Filter भएको glucose सामान्यतया sodium-glucose transporters मार्फत proximal convoluted tubule मा धेरैजसो पुनःशोषित हुन्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Renal Physiology","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK538339/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which cranial nerve is responsible for most facial expression muscles?","अनुहारका अधिकांश expression muscles लाई कुन cranial nerve ले नियन्त्रण गर्छ?",["Facial nerve (VII)","Trigeminal nerve (V)","Oculomotor nerve (III)","Vagus nerve (X)"],0,"The facial nerve (cranial nerve VII) supplies the muscles of facial expression; the trigeminal nerve supplies muscles of mastication.","Facial nerve (cranial nerve VII) ले अनुहारका expression muscles लाई nerve supply दिन्छ; trigeminal nerve ले चपाउने मांसपेशीलाई supply गर्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Neuroanatomy, Cranial Nerves","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK11100/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which cells produce pulmonary surfactant?","फोक्सोमा pulmonary surfactant कुन कोषिकाले उत्पादन गर्छ?",["Type II alveolar cells","Type I alveolar cells","Alveolar macrophages","Ciliated bronchial cells"],0,"Type II alveolar cells secrete surfactant, which reduces surface tension and helps prevent alveolar collapse.","Type II alveolar cells ले surfactant उत्पादन गर्छन्, जसले surface tension घटाएर alveoli खुम्चिनबाट जोगाउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Physiology, Pulmonary","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482502/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which blood component is primarily responsible for oxygen transport?","अक्सिजन बोक्ने मुख्य जिम्मेवारी कुन blood component को हो?",["Haemoglobin in red blood cells","Platelets","Plasma albumin","Neutrophils"],0,"Haemoglobin in red blood cells binds and transports most oxygen in the blood.","Red blood cells भित्रको haemoglobin ले रगतमा धेरैजसो oxygen बाँधेर बोक्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: Components of the Blood","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/18-1-an-overview-of-blood",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Which division of the autonomic nervous system generally increases heart rate during a fight-or-flight response?","Fight-or-flight अवस्थामा सामान्यतया कुन autonomic nervous system ले heart rate बढाउँछ?",["Sympathetic division","Parasympathetic division","Somatic sensory division","Enteric sensory pathway only"],0,"Sympathetic activation increases heart rate and supports the fight-or-flight response; parasympathetic activity generally slows the heart.","Sympathetic activation ले heart rate बढाएर fight-or-flight प्रतिक्रिया दिन्छ; parasympathetic गतिविधिले सामान्यतया मुटुको गति घटाउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax Anatomy & Physiology: Autonomic Nervous System","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/15-1-divisions-of-the-autonomic-nervous-system",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );

 // Diagram-based Anatomy & Physiology practice: text diagrams remain readable on mobile.
 practiceQ.push(
  ["Study the heart pathway: SA node → [A] → Bundle of His → bundle branches → Purkinje fibres. Which structure is [A]?","मुटुको मार्ग हेर्नुहोस्: SA node → [A] → Bundle of His → bundle branches → Purkinje fibres। [A] कुन संरचना हो?",["Atrioventricular (AV) node","Sinoatrial (SA) node","Aorta","Mitral valve"],0,"The AV node receives the impulse from the SA node and briefly delays conduction before the impulse travels through the Bundle of His.","AV node ले SA node बाट impulse लिएर Bundle of His हुँदै अघि बढ्नुअघि केही समय ढिलाइ गराउँछ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax: Cardiac muscle and electrical activity","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/19-2-cardiac-muscle-and-electrical-activity",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Label the nephron flow: Glomerulus → Bowman's capsule → [A] → Loop of Henle → DCT → Collecting duct. What is [A]?","Nephron को मार्ग: Glomerulus → Bowman's capsule → [A] → Loop of Henle → DCT → Collecting duct। [A] कुन भाग हो?",["Proximal convoluted tubule (PCT)","Distal convoluted tubule (DCT)","Ureter","Renal pelvis"],0,"The proximal convoluted tubule follows Bowman's capsule and is the major site of reabsorption of filtered water and solutes.","Bowman's capsule पछि PCT आउँछ र filter भएका पानी तथा solutes को धेरैजसो reabsorption यहीँ हुन्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Renal Physiology","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK538339/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Diagram: Inspiration → thoracic volume [A] → intrapulmonary pressure [B] → air moves IN. Which pair correctly fills [A] and [B]?","चित्र: Inspiration → thoracic volume [A] → intrapulmonary pressure [B] → हावा भित्र जान्छ। [A] र [B] को सही जोडी कुन हो?",["Increases; decreases","Decreases; increases","Increases; increases","Decreases; decreases"],0,"During inspiration, thoracic volume increases and intrapulmonary pressure falls below atmospheric pressure, drawing air into the lungs.","सास भित्र तान्दा thoracic volume बढ्छ र intrapulmonary pressure घट्छ; त्यसैले हावा फोक्सोभित्र पस्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax: The respiratory system","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/22-3-the-process-of-breathing",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Reflex arc diagram: Receptor → [A] neuron → spinal cord → motor neuron → muscle. Which neuron is [A]?","Reflex arc: Receptor → [A] neuron → spinal cord → motor neuron → muscle। [A] कुन neuron हो?",["Sensory (afferent) neuron","Motor (efferent) neuron","Interneuron only","Autonomic ganglion"],0,"The sensory or afferent neuron carries information from the receptor toward the central nervous system.","Sensory वा afferent neuron ले receptor बाट सूचना central nervous system तर्फ लैजान्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax: The nervous system","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/13-1-the-structure-and-function-of-the-nervous-system",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["Endocrine axis: Hypothalamus (TRH) → [A] (TSH) → Thyroid (T3/T4). Which organ is [A]?","Endocrine मार्ग: Hypothalamus (TRH) → [A] (TSH) → Thyroid (T3/T4)। [A] कुन अंग हो?",["Anterior pituitary gland","Adrenal cortex","Pancreas","Parathyroid gland"],0,"TRH stimulates the anterior pituitary to release TSH; TSH then stimulates the thyroid gland.","TRH ले anterior pituitary लाई TSH निकाल्न उत्तेजित गर्छ; TSH ले thyroid gland लाई उत्तेजित गर्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Physiology, Thyroid Hormone","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK285545/",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
 mockQ.push(
  ["Which sequence correctly shows normal cardiac electrical conduction?","मुटुको सामान्य electrical conduction को सही क्रम कुन हो?",["SA node → AV node → Bundle of His → bundle branches → Purkinje fibres","AV node → SA node → Purkinje fibres → Bundle of His","Purkinje fibres → SA node → AV node → bundle branches","SA node → Purkinje fibres → AV node → Bundle of His"],0,"The normal sequence begins at the SA node, passes through the AV node, then the His-Purkinje conduction system.","सामान्य क्रम SA node बाट सुरु भई AV node र त्यसपछि His-Purkinje conduction system हुँदै जान्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax: Cardiac muscle and electrical activity","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/19-2-cardiac-muscle-and-electrical-activity",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["In the nephron diagram, which segment is the main site of bulk reabsorption? Bowman's capsule → PCT → Loop of Henle → DCT → Collecting duct.","Nephron चित्रमा धेरैजसो पदार्थ पुनःशोषण हुने मुख्य भाग कुन हो? Bowman's capsule → PCT → Loop of Henle → DCT → Collecting duct।",["Proximal convoluted tubule","Distal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct","Loop of Henle only"],0,"The proximal convoluted tubule performs the largest share of reabsorption of filtered water, electrolytes and nutrients.","Filter भएका पानी, electrolytes र पोषक तत्त्वको सबैभन्दा ठूलो हिस्सा proximal convoluted tubule मा पुनःशोषण हुन्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Renal Physiology","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK538339/",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["During quiet expiration, which change normally occurs?","सामान्य सास बाहिर फाल्दा कुन परिवर्तन हुन्छ?",["Thoracic volume decreases and intrapulmonary pressure rises","Thoracic volume increases and pressure falls","Diaphragm contracts and moves downward","Air enters because lung pressure falls"],0,"Quiet expiration is usually passive: thoracic volume decreases, intrapulmonary pressure rises and air flows out.","सामान्य expiration प्रायः passive हुन्छ: thoracic volume घट्छ, फोक्सोभित्रको pressure बढ्छ र हावा बाहिर निस्कन्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax: The respiratory system","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/22-3-the-process-of-breathing",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["In the reflex arc Receptor → sensory neuron → CNS → motor neuron → [A], what is [A]?","Reflex arc Receptor → sensory neuron → CNS → motor neuron → [A] मा [A] कुन हो?",["Effector (muscle or gland)","Receptor","Sensory ganglion","Thalamus"],0,"The effector, usually a muscle or gland, carries out the response after receiving the motor signal.","Motor signal पाएपछि प्रतिक्रिया गर्ने भाग effector हो, जुन सामान्यतया muscle वा gland हुन्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["OpenStax: The nervous system","https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/13-1-the-structure-and-function-of-the-nervous-system",false,"2026-11-25"]],
  ["When circulating T3 and T4 rise, what normally happens through negative feedback?","रगतमा T3 र T4 बढ्दा negative feedback मार्फत सामान्यतया के हुन्छ?",["TRH and TSH secretion decrease","TRH and TSH secretion both increase","Only insulin secretion stops","The thyroid stops responding permanently"],0,"Higher circulating thyroid hormones suppress hypothalamic TRH and pituitary TSH secretion through negative feedback.","रगतमा thyroid hormone बढ्दा negative feedback का कारण hypothalamus को TRH र pituitary को TSH secretion घट्छ।","Anatomy & Physiology",["NCBI Bookshelf: Physiology, Thyroid Hormone","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK285545/",false,"2026-11-25"]]
 );
